# Dual remote push

When the user says **push git** / **پوش گیت** (or equivalent):

1. Commit only if they asked to commit, or if uncommitted work must ship with an explicit push of current work — never commit secrets (`.env`).
2. Push **both** remotes on the current branch:
   - `origin` → GitHub (`https://github.com/vilanovax/superhesab.git` or current `origin` URL)
   - `hamgit` → `git@hamgit.ir:ramtinica/superhesab.git`
3. If `hamgit` remote is missing: `git remote add hamgit git@hamgit.ir:ramtinica/superhesab.git`
4. Prefer: `git push -u origin HEAD` then `git push -u hamgit HEAD` (or equivalent). Report both results.
5. Do **not** treat a single-remote push as done when the user said push git.
